rs still  be concerned about getting into the  stock and the Saudi market the  international investors will be watching  this very closely again it's the world's  most profitable company the biggest  crude exporter it has its IPO its debut  has made a new record a bigger than  Alibaba which was which held the  previous record so on a lot of metrics  it is a company that will be very  closely watched by the international  investors probably more out of a fear of  missing out on something that might be  good but by and large so far the  international investors interest has  been very tepid to say the least  that was one of the reasons even in the  final days Saudi Arabia cancelled the  international road shows up a plant for  four US and Europe and Asia so but will  they will they keep an eye they will  probably but with the valuation that has  been achieved with us very limited  offering in the domestic market is  probably not evaluation that the  international investors will go by they  have their own estimates which until now  have been pretty much lower than where  the the valuation is suggested as of as  of today so so will the Saudis in your  view achieve their goal of diversifying  their economy with the proceeds from  this IPO so as I mentioned the proceeds  have been much smaller than they might  have expected we just had the Saudi  budget announced earlier this week and  clearly they're looking at a bigger  budget deficit they're looking at much  lesser oil revenues already oil revenues  in 2019 came in nearly 10 percent below  what they had budgeted so all of those  are going to be major concerns they will  need to be looking for more money will  it help in the diversification efforts  yes probably but not but not as much as  it would have let's say had they managed  to raise a hundred billion dollars  instead of twenty six billion thank you  so much for your insight  Donna Hari who's a global oil market  analyst joining us there from Singapore  thank you f